---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description="Twelve weeks on the design of delay, from the gap between clock time and felt time to the question of who is asked to wait."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Every system you use has decided how long you will wait and what you will
    be told while you do. This course treats that decision as design work: the
    thresholds, the progress indicators, the hold scripts, the queues, and the
    politics of who is asked to wait. You will log your own waits, take one
    apart, and redesign a wait you are not permitted to shorten.
  </p>
  <p>
    The lecture is Tuesday and the workshop is Thursday, every week. Weeks 1 to
    6 build the techniques and weeks 7 to 12 ask who they are pointed at.
  </p>
  <p>
    Teaching stops for a fortnight after week 6 and resumes on 12 April. A
    course about waiting has a two week gap in the middle of it, and that is
    the only time this page will mention it.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
